    "$comment":  "Bravo buttons: the trim wheel, autopilot panel, gear lever and the seven switches. Two halves. \u0027controls\u0027 is the PHYSICAL map - which button number each control is - and it is MEASURED by Probe-HoneycombDevices.ps1 -Capture, never typed in: \u0027prober\u0027 is the number the prober prints (Windows\u0027 1-based count), \u0027fsuipc\u0027 is FSUIPC\u0027s number for the same button (prober - 1, and above 31 FSUIPC reports from 132), and \u0027verified\u0027 is true only after the capture has seen it pressed. Set-BravoButtons.ps1 refuses to write any control that is not verified. \u0027map\u0027 is the CHOICE of what each control does in the sim - control numbers from the Controls List that ships with FSUIPC - and it is a decision to review, not a measurement. Switches send explicit ON on press and OFF on release rather than a toggle, so the switch position and the sim always agree. The INCR/DECR rotary depends on the mode selector: FSUIPC compound conditions, one line per mode.",
    "schemaVersion":  1,
